    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned the owner identity key to `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and wired all duplicate detection through it.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 `key(telephone, email, lastName)` now returns the lower-case SHA-256 hex of `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)` (was a plain `tel|email|householdId` string). Added a standard American Soundex implementation (`soundex`) and a private `sha256hex` helper. Email is normalized inside `key`; `householdId(...)` is retained unchanged (still used for household size/membership).\n\n- **`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 the 409 check now compares the new SHA-256 key (built from lastName's soundex, not householdId), still skipping soft-deleted owners; the blocklist still runs first via the earlier `normalizeEmail` step. Two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones now get distinct keys and are no longer rejected.\n\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft-match now triggers when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` both match (was: same lastName + postcode + different telephone), still recording the lowest matching id and skipping deleted/`sharesHousehold` owners.\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the returned `identityKey` mapping now derives from `lastName` (soundex) instead of `householdId`, so the response key matches the detection key.\n\n- Doc/spec updates in `DuplicateIdentityException`, `openapi.yml`, and `owners.POST.yml` comments to describe the new key.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` \u2014 64-hex shape \u2014 and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 409 on identical identity) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
